verses.text:
Gilboa’s mountains, let no dew or rain land on you,
and let your slopes yield no offerings!{f}
On you the hero’s shield lay filthy,
Saul’s shield, left without its oil.{g}

“You rescued me from the quarrels of my own people.{i}
You kept me as ruler over nations.
Strangers I never knew now serve me.

He gives his king great victories{k}
and stays loyal to his chosen one,
to David and his family forever.”
